            </td>\n110:             <td>${item.manufacturer || 'N/A'}</td>\n111:             <td class=\"font-monospace small\">${item.batchNumber || 'N/A'}</td>\n112:             <td>\n113:               <span class=\"badge ${item.type === 'PURCHASE' ? 'bg-success' : 'bg-primary'}\">${item.type}</span>\n114:             </td>\n115:             <td>\n116:               <span class=\"status-pill match\">${item.verificationStatus}</span>\n117:             </td>\n118:             <td>${item.pharmacyName || '<span class=\"text-muted small\">MedCheck BD Search</span>'}</td>\n119:             <td class=\"small text-muted\">${formatDate(item.checkedAt)}</td>\n120:             <td class=\"text-end\">\n121:               ${item.medicineId ? `\n122:                 <a href=\"medicine-details.html?id=${item.medicineId._id || item.medicineId}\" class=\"btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm py-0 px-2 me-1\">\n123:                   View\n124:                 </a>\n125:               ` : ''}\n126:               <button class=\"btn btn-outline-danger btn-sm py-0 px-2\" onclick=\"deleteHistoryItem('${item._id}')\">\n127:                 <i class=\"fas fa-trash-alt\"></i>\n128:               </button>\n129:             </td>\n130:           </tr>\n131:         `).join('');\n132:       } catch (err) {\n133:         showToast(err.message, 'danger');\n134:       }\n135:     }\n136: \n137:     async function deleteHistoryItem(id) {\n138:       try {\n139:         const res = await fetch(`/api/history/${id}`, {\n140:           method: 'DELETE',\n141:           headers: getAuthHeaders(),\n142:         });\n143:         const data = await res.json();\n144:         if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.message);\n145: \n146:         showToast('Record deleted from history', 'info');\n147:         loadCustomerHistory();\n148:       } catch (err) {\n149:         showToast(err.message, 'danger');\n150:       }\n151:     }\n152: \n153:     async function clearAllHistory() {\n154:       if (!confirm('Are you sure you want to clear your entire medicine history?')) return;\n155: \n156:       try {\n157:         const res = await fetch('/api/history', {\n158:           method: 'DELETE',\n159:           headers: getAuthHeaders(),\n160:         });\n161:         const data = await res.json();\n162:         if (!res.ok) throw new Error(data.message);\n163: \n164:         showToast('History cleared successfully', 'info');\n165:         loadCustomerHistory();\n166:       } catch (err) {\n167:         showToast(err.message, 'danger');\n168:       }\n169:     }\n170:   </script>\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":506,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:16:00Z","thinking":"**Examining Authentication Handling**\n\nObserving that a 401 status triggers token and user data removal from local storage.  The code then indicates a potential prompt or redirect for guest access.  The current logic handles unauthenticated states, indicating a check for a token before proceeding.\n\n\n**Evaluating History Loading Logic**\n\nThe code presents two scenarios for the history display: successful retrieval and error handling. The success case renders the data while the error scenario presents a user-friendly message. An expired session results in a login prompt and display. A retry button also appears in case of an error.\n\n\n**Analyzing Medicine History Logic**\n\nThe system allows customers to save verified medicine to their history, recording details like medicine ID, name, and batch number. The backend code conditionally saves this data if the user is authenticated and has a customer role.  Considering the code, it is important to investigate whether the backend provides feedback to the frontend after saving.\n\n\n**Implementing Medicine History Synchronization**\n\nThe backend now explicitly indicates if medicine history was saved for a customer, which informs frontend display. The frontend uses this flag to show success or login prompt. Independently, the verified medicine is also saved to local storage, ensuring that the history is preserved even for guest users.\n\n**Reviewing Authentication Handling**\n\nA concern is whether an expired token triggers data loss in local storage, which would include the medicine history. It is necessary to examine how `enforceRoleGuard` handles these scenarios and whether this causes any data inconsistencies or loss.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd\\server\\routes\\auth.js","toolAction":"View auth.js routes","toolSummary":"View server/routes/auth.js"}}]}
