{"step_index":517,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:22:20Z","thinking":"**Assessing Website's Medicine Purchase**\n\nThe user inquires about medicine purchases and the location of the purchase option on the website. This suggests a potential e-commerce functionality focused on medications. Alternatively, the user is only asking for a checking facility.\n\n\n**Identifying Missing Purchase Feature**\n\nThe system design specifies a direct customer purchase flow, but the current implementation only allows pharmacy-initiated sales. No customer-facing option exists to \"Order,\" \"Buy,\" or \"Reserve\" medications. The missing feature creates a purchase/order record linked to the customer and the chosen pharmacy.\n\n\n**Defining Purchase Integration Points**\n\nThe purchase flow must integrate into multiple customer-facing pages: pharmacy details, verification results, and price comparison. Each page requires a prominent \"Buy/Order\" button. The customer selection initiates a checkout modal.\n\nThe checkout modal will handle medicine specifics and pharmacy information. A digital receipt and purchase history will be generated upon completion, and the pharmacy inventory is reduced.\n\n\n**Designing the Checkout Flow**\n\nThe checkout process will have medicine quantity and price selection with a dynamic subtotal. Customer information (name, phone, delivery details) and payment options (multiple digital payment methods, cash on delivery) must be included. A \"Confirm Order & Pay\" button will initiate order processing.\n\nA successful order will call the relevant API endpoint to record the purchase, deduct inventory, generate a receipt and update customer's purchase history. Order confirmation will immediately display with a receipt link and a medicine history link.\n\n**Implementing History Persistence Fixes**\n\nAddress history persistence issues using auto-healing sessions via a \"session expired\" login button. Also 