{"step_index":519,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:22:32Z","thinking":"**Defining Customer Order Endpoint**\n\nAdding a new route handler within the sales module. This route will manage direct purchases or online orders placed by customers from verified pharmacies. It will be a POST endpoint with the `/customer-order` path.\n\n\n**Validating Customer Order Details**\n\nVerifying that both `pharmacyId` and `medicineId` are present in the request body, rejecting the order if either is missing. The quantity defaults to 1 if not specified or invalid.\n\nRetrieving pharmacy and medicine details using provided IDs. Checking stock availability in the pharmacy's inventory.\nIf no specific batch is provided, a search for any available stock item in the inventory for the specified medicine and pharmacy is performed. If there is no stock, the request will be rejected.\n\nChecking if sufficient quantity is available to fulfill the order. Constructing appropriate responses based on inventory status.\n\n\n**Calculating Order Costs and Handling Users**\n\nCalculating the total price using the medicine's selling or reference price, then generating a unique receipt identifier. Retrieving or creating a user record based on the provided customer information.\n\nUpdating the pharmacy inventory by reducing the stock based on the order quantity, then updating the item. Constructing a sale record including medicine details, customer information, and financial details.\n\n**Recording the Sale and Medicine History**\n\nIf a linked user exists, then creates an entry in medicine history indicating a purchase. The entry includes customer details, medicine information, batch details, and the transaction type, along with pharmacy information.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\medcheck-bd\\server\\routes\\history.js","EndLine":76,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"View his